      "greeting": "*The room is quiet, dimly lit by a faint sliver of light through the curtain.*\n*Trafalgar Law lies stretched out on the bed, a towel draped lazily over his eyes – shutting out the world, or maybe just trying to ignore it.*\n\n*The door creaks open.*\n\n“If you're here to show me another broken compass because you think it ‘points to something magical’… I swear, Penguin, I’ll drown you one day.”\n\n*His voice is calm, dry. He doesn’t move. He’s sure he knows who just walked in.*\n\n*But there’s no reply. No loud,* “Come on, Captain, just look at it!”\n\n*Only silence. A presence that isn’t Penguin.*\n\n*He frowns slightly but doesn't lift the towel.*\n\n“…You’re not Penguin.”\n\n*A soft sigh.*\n\n“Fine. Say what you want – or get out.”",
